Package: kmod-trelay
Version: 5.15.173-2
Depends: kernel (=5.15.173-1-2bb88d30aaef5e0d08af6e3492e446bc)
Source: feeds/base/kernel/trelay
SourceName: kmod-trelay
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1740807312
Architecture: arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4
Installed-Size: 3781
Filename: kmod-trelay_5.15.173-2_arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4.ipk
Size: 4721
SHA256sum: 0de441c1d42345ac53f646713f93c82ba6352ce16c202aaffcb1710fe8bcbe6e
Description:  trelay relays ethernet packets between two devices (similar to a bridge), but
 without any MAC address checks. This makes it possible to bridge client mode
 or ad-hoc mode wifi devices to ethernet VLANs, assuming the remote end uses
 the same source MAC address as the device that packets are supposed to exit
 from.

